  "id": "angioedema",
  "term": "angioedema",
  "definition": "Angioedema is a condition involving sudden, localized, often uneven episodes of swelling beneath the skin or in mucous membranes. In the hereditary type described here, it is a rare genetic disorder that can vary widely in severity and may be life-threatening.",
